.SH RETURN VALUE
Except for
.BR \%flushinp ","
functions that return integers return
.B ERR
upon failure and
.B OK
upon success.
.PP
Functions that return pointers return a null pointer on failure.
.PP
In
.IR \%ncurses ","
.bP
.B \%flushinp
returns
.B ERR
if the terminal was not initialized,
and
.bP
.B \%putwin
returns
.B ERR
if its associated \fIwrite\fP(2) calls return
.BR ERR "."
